This is the complete wiring diagram for the architecture defined in your GitHub repository and past conversation: 2S (7.4V) Battery Pack charging from a 5V Type-C connection, stepped down to 5V, and including the physical button circuit.
Important Disclaimers before you begin:
Safety First: Lithium-ion batteries are dangerous if mistreated. Ensure all wires are properly insulated. Do not short the battery leads.
Buck Converter Adjustment: CRITICAL! You must connect the 7.4V battery pack to the Buck converter input and use a multimeter to adjust the screw potentiometer until the output reads exactly 5.0V BEFORE you connect the output wires to the ESP32-CAM. If you omit this step, you will instantly fry your microcontroller.
The 2S Charger: You cannot use TP4056 modules for this series configuration from a single Type-C port. You must use a dedicated 2S Lithium Boost Charger/BMS Board designed for 5V Type-C input (e.g., boards based on the IP2326 or TP5100).
